    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nMagdala House is an exceptional and beautifully extended detached family residence, enviably positioned along the prestigious Castleknock Road in the very heart of Castleknock Village. Behind elegant electric gates, this distinguished home offers a rare combination of elegance, contemporary luxury and outstanding family accommodation, extending to approximately 325 sq.m (3,498 sq.ft).\n\nPresented in turnkey condition and finished to an exacting standard throughout, the property seamlessly blends refined interiors with modern family living. Boasting an impressive BER rating of (INSERT BER), the accommodation is both energy efficient and exquisitely appointed. With five generously proportioned bedrooms, including three en-suite bedrooms, the residence is perfectly configured for growing families seeking both space and convenience. A welcoming entrance hall, flooded with natural light from the striking atrium above, sets the tone for the elegant accommodation within. To one side, a gracious drawing room features a marble fireplace and attractive bay window, while opposite, a formal dining room echoes the same sense of elegance with its own marble fireplace and bay window. Double doors open to the heart of this home, the open-plan kitchen and breakfast room, complete with a country style kitchen with range cooker and delightful views across the landscaped gardens. A separate utility room provides excellent practicality. To the rear of the breakfast room lies a magnificent family room with vaulted ceilings and feature skylights, creating an impressive space for everyday living and entertaining. French doors open directly onto the sun-drenched patio and gardens beyond. Further accommodation on the ground floor includes a guest WC and a spacious guest bedroom (bedroom 3) with en-suite shower room. Upstairs, the luxurious principal suite enjoys a private en-suite bathroom and walk-in wardrobe. A second bedroom also benefits from a walk-in dressing room and en-suite bathroom, while two further generously sized bedrooms with fitted wardrobes are served by a beautifully appointed family bathroom.\n\nThe magnificent south-west facing rear garden is a particular feature of this exceptional home. Thoughtfully designed to create a private outdoor sanctuary, it offers an abundance of space for both family enjoyment and elegant entertaining. Extensive sandstone terraces and a raised paved seating area provide the perfect setting for al fresco dining, while the manicured lawn is framed by mature trees, specimen planting and beautifully stocked borders. A versatile garden room/workshop offers excellent additional storage or hobby space, and gated side access provides convenient connectivity to the front of the property.\n\nMagdala House is enviably situated along the main Castleknock Road and is within walking distance of 3 primary schools. Castleknock Village shops, restaurants, pubs and churches are located within a five-minute walk, as is Castleknock Tennis Club. The magnificent Phoenix Park is 10-minute walk. City Centre is just 8km. Castleknock Train Station is a 6-minute walk. There is an excellent bus service (Dublin Bus Route 37 & 38) within a 1min walk. There is unrivalled access to the N3, M3 and M50, which in turn gives access to other major destinations. Dublin Airport is a 20-minute drive approx.\n\nMagdala House represents a rare opportunity to acquire a landmark family home of exceptional quality and scale in one of Dublin 15's most sought-after and established residential addresses."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 5m x 3.9m\nImpressive entrance hallway with double height ceilings and feature solid Oak staircase to gallery landing. Tiled flooring.\n\nLiving Room - 7.4m x 5.1m\nTo the right of the main hallway large living room with feature marble fireplace with brick inlay. Bay window.\n\nDining Room - 7.4m x 5.1m\nTo the left of the main hallway double doors lead to a formal dining room with feature marble fireplace (gas fire) with brick inlay. Bay window. Solid walnut timber flooring. French doors to kitchen.\n\nKitchen/Breakfast Room - 9.43m x 3.2m\nThe heart of this home is the l-shaped kitchen/breakfast room. There is a solid wood fully fitted country style timber kitchen with hand painted cream units and black granite worktops. Feature range with granite backsplash. Integrated fridge/freezer and dishwasher, Tiled flooring. Open plan to breakfast/dining area with double doors leading to the rear patio and garden.\n\nUtility Room - 3.2m x 2.5m\nGood sized utility with fitted worktops and storage presses, stainless steel sink. Plumbed for washing machine and dryer. Tiled flooring.\n\nFamily Room - 6.2m x 5.5m\nA very well proportioned and bright family room located to the rear of the house, feature vaulted ceilings, entertainment wall with solid fuel stove, double doors lead to the rear garden and patio. 2 x Velux roof lights.\n\nCorridor - 3.6m x 1.1m\nTiled flooring.\n\nGuest WC - 2m x 1.1m\nComprising of wc and wash hand basin, fully tiled.\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.2m x 3.2m\nDouble bedroomwith fitted wardrobes, located on the ground floor. Oak timber flooring.\n\nEn-Suite - 2m x 2m\nFully tiled comprises of a shower, wc and wash hand basin.\n\nLanding - 8.3m x 3m\nFeature staircase with large roof light allowing for plenty of natural light.\n\nPrimary Bedroom - 5.1m x 4.1m\nLarge double bedroom t the front of the property.\n\nEn-Suite - 2.8m x 2m\nFully tiled contains jacuzzi bath, wc and wash hand basin.\n\nWalk in wardrobe - 4m x 1.5m\nWith fitted shelving and fashion rails. Feature port window.\n\nBedroom 2 - 5m x 3.6m\nLarge double bedroom to the front of the house. Oak timber flooring.\n\nWalk in wardrobe - 3.1m x 1.5m\nWith fitted shelving and fashion rails.\n\nEn-Suite - 2m x 2m\nFully tiled contains jacuzzi bath, wc and wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 4 - 5m x 2.8m\nDouble bedroom with built in closet, oak timber flooring.\n\nBedroom 5 - 5m x 2.8m\nDouble bedroom with built in closet, oak timber flooring.\n\nBathroom - 2.8m x 2m\nFully tiled contains jacuzzi bath, wc and wash hand basin.\n\nGarden shed - 3.7m x 2m\nIdeal for home storage and as a workshop, power supply.\n\n"
